      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "TEQUILA BABY (2) makes her stable debut for the Kendrick's and shoulders strong NSW form. Has been patchy this prep but her peaks are superior. Drops back to 1000m off 41 days and gets in a treat after McColm's 3kg claim. Will take some beating if she's on-song. SHAKO (1) is the proven local danger, with a close CL5 third at this track last start and an excellent track-and-trip record. DREAM LANTERN (5) resumes with two handy Doomben trial wins behind her, so expecting her to be forward enough to give this a shake. SWEET HESITATION (4) was sound first-up here when sticking on soundly into the placings. Fitter and gets weight relief over a trip she relishes. Not underestimating. I MISS MARGIE (8) hasn't won for a long time but drops back from stronger and has peaks that can threaten. Keeping safe in minors.",
